    "body": "## Summary\n- allow the assigned worker to upload `PARTICIPANTS` attachments only while a job is exactly `IN_PROGRESS`\n- keep worker uploads private to job participants; workers cannot create `JOB_VIEWERS` or `EXECUTION_SECRET` attachments\n- preserve receipt/evidence history through the existing immutable-after-assignment deletion policy\n- extend focused policy tests and the container attachment smoke for before/after-assignment boundaries and historical receipt access\n- document the new lifecycle and privacy rules\n\n## Why\nExpense reimbursement needs trustworthy receipt/evidence attachments from the worker. The existing attachment model allowed uploads only from the requester, so building expense claims on top of it would either be impossible or require a broader unsafe permission. This slice creates the narrow prerequisite: assigned-worker evidence is participant-only, execution-phase-only, and immutable after upload.\n\n## Migration\nNo Flyway migration is required; the existing attachment schema already records uploader identity and visibility.\n\n## Validation\nDo not merge until all latest-head required CI/checks complete successfully.",
